content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 4.2 mm/s against Figure 3 zones (velocity, mm/s RMS, on bearing housings): this is Zone B (2.8–4.5, 'long-term operation'). It is 0.3 mm/s below the Zone C boundary (4.5, 'restricted – plan maintenance') and below the Zone D stop limit (7.1). The highest reading from both housings must be used.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 74 C against the HF-300 limits (normal up to 70 C; alarm 80 C; trip 90 C): this is above normal but below alarm and trip. The limit is measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Grinding noise at the non-drive-end bearing (6310-C3, HF3-510). The manual requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. That criterion is met by the noise and by the above-normal temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal reported 'dry'. If this means no leakage, there is no seal fault. If it means the seal is running without flush, that breaks the manual requirement: Plan 11 flush from pump discharge, never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No reading reaches a stop limit: vibration is not in Zone D and temperature is not at the 90 C trip. Plan the maintenance rather than stopping immediately. Stop the pump if vibration reaches 7.1 mm/s or temperature reaches the 80 C alarm or 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: wear of the non-drive-end bearing. Grinding noise, above-normal housing temperature and vibration near the top of Zone B all fit bearing wear, which is listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment, listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing, a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, listed causes of high vibration. These are less consistent with noise localised to the bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Schedule a planned outage. Until then, monitor both bearing housings: classify the highest vibration reading against Figure 3 and check housing temperature against the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Escalate to an immediate stop if either is reached.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm whether 'seal is dry' means no leakage or loss of seal flush. Verify that the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge is working. The seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check grease quantity in the bearing housings, since over-greasing is a cause of high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. Casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: the non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510) and the drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512). Inspect the impeller and shaft while the assembly is out.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit a new seal unless it is found damaged or has to be disturbed. If it is replaced, fit component seal HF3-450 per section 5.2, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and tighten the seal gland nuts (M10) to 25 Nm per Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with a new casing gasket HF3-120, which must be replaced whenever the casing is opened. Tighten fasteners to Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft after the bearing housing work. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, confirm that the seal flush is working. Record vibration on both housings, aiming for Zone A (below 2.8 mm/s), and confirm housing temperature is at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replaced as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type – contingency only, if found damaged (correct part for serial below HF3-22000)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump and its 55 kW, 400 V motor, then drain the pump before any work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before and after restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration enters Zone D (7.1 mm/s or more) or bearing temperature reaches the 90 C trip. Treat 80 C as the alarm level.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency, only if the seal must be replaced: mechanical seal replacement 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B and sets 30 Nm gland torque. It applies only to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is serial HF3-21100, which is below that range. Therefore the bulletin does not apply: use HF3-450, the manual parts list and Table 5 (seal gland nuts 25 Nm).",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin's sleeve criterion (replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm) is stated for affected serials only. The manual says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring, with no numeric limit. That limit therefore cannot be assumed for this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no leakage, or that the seal or flush is running dry?",
    "Is 4.2 mm/s the highest reading of the two bearing housings, and what is the vibration and temperature trend?",
    "The manual gives no step-by-step bearing removal or fitting procedure. Is removing the impeller and seal required to replace the bearings?",
    "Grease type and correct fill quantity for the bearings are not given in the evidence.",
    "There is no numeric sleeve-scoring rejection limit for pumps below serial HF3-22000; HF3-455 availability may be needed if scoring is found.",
    "Coupling or motor fastener torques, if the motor is moved for alignment, are not covered."
  ]
}
